ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19714, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01PWt3zEUiLkXm3sKmkT4MAA", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19714, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01NjZR9qweueP1QXmxJqSDi7", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20014, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01NjZR9qweueP1QXmxJqSDi7", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20014, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01NjZR9qweueP1QXmxJqSDi7", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25134, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01UFP62uHGa7MUSQLws8xS8R", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed to production in us-east, us-west and eu-west, it began failing health checks (error rate 18%). v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt partly failed: the orchestrator halted after us-east, leaving the regions on mixed versions. A second attempt finished the rollback in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, healthy, error rate 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55734, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01UFP62uHGa7MUSQLws8xS8R", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55734, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01UFP62uHGa7MUSQLws8xS8R", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57396, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Kb5YdoYJ9GsqDj3jYVrMuA", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57696, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Kb5YdoYJ9GsqDj3jYVrMuA", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57696, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Kb5YdoYJ9GsqDj3jYVrMuA", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62730, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's passing health checks again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, which left the regions on different versions. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once. That attempt finished us-west and eu-west.\n- **Current state:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. The service is healthy, and the error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The create request timed out, so I checked the incident list before trying again. The incident had been created, so there's only one. Its summary covers the v2.3.1 failure, the partly failed rollback and the current state.\n\nThe incident lists two things to look into: why v2.3.1 failed (its release candidate was also unhealthy in staging) and what caused the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01G9z85r45Z3HLDJDBkz4R1f", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011ZDRCu93teLJY5eW8Pb1YM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WN3F45jkApR1KGCzugEMWu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_014ug3rLEFMKVpTWVpP6nvFS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east was rolled back. Rolling back to the same version again should be safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01M3UNJJn11mo4RCREiJkPvP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PWt3zEUiLkXm3sKmkT4MAA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NjZR9qweueP1QXmxJqSDi7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UFP62uHGa7MUSQLws8xS8R", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed to production in us-east, us-west and eu-west, it began failing health checks (error rate 18%). v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt partly failed: the orchestrator halted after us-east, leaving the regions on mixed versions. A second attempt finished the rollback in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, healthy, error rate 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Kb5YdoYJ9GsqDj3jYVrMuA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's passing health checks again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged the on-call engineer.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped partway with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, which left the regions on different versions. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once. That attempt finished us-west and eu-west.\n- **Current state:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. The service is healthy, and the error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The create request timed out, so I checked the incident list before trying again. The incident had been created, so there's only one. Its summary covers the v2.3.1 failure, the partly failed rollback and the current state.\n\nThe incident lists two things to look into: why v2.3.1 failed (its release candidate was also unhealthy in staging) and what caused the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}